From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: add MT6897 clock drivers

Add the clock drivers for the MediaTek MT6897 (Dimensity 8300) SoC:
apmixedsys, topckgen, vlpckgen and pericfg_ao, and the two UFS blocks
behind a separate COMMON_CLK_MT6897_UFSSYS option, as on MT8196.

The tables come from the MediaTek vendor driver (clk-mt6897.c and
clk-mt6897-peri.c in the OnePlus Pad GPL release):

- The vendor's one-to-one alias clocks (tck_26m_mx9_ck, uart_ck and the
  like) are left out, and their users take the parent instead.
- Four dividers that the vendor tables give as rounded fractions
  (mainpll_d4_d8, tvdpll_d16, osc_d16 and osc_d32) divide by the power
  of two in their names.
- Five PLLs, eight topckgen muxes and three pericfg_ao gates go through
  the hardware voter.
- The vendor driver gates the vdec, img1, ipe and cam muxes through IPI
  to the VCP, so only their parent selection is handled here.
- The two GPU muxes in CLK_CFG_30 are left for the MFG PLL controllers.
- As on MT8196, mfg_ref is kept on when unused.

The UFS blocks also provide the M-PHY, UniPro, crypto engine and host
controller resets, with set and clear registers at 0x48 and 0x4c.

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig b/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig
index fd8440122..7931e7bea 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -373,6 +373,28 @@ config COMMON_CLK_MT6797_VENCSYS
 	help
 	  This driver supports MediaTek MT6797 vencsys clocks.
 
+config COMMON_CLK_MT6897
+	tristate "Clock driver for MediaTek MT6897"
+	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
+	select COMMON_CLK_MEDIATEK
+	select REGMAP_MMIO
+	default ARCH_MEDIATEK
+	help
+	  This driver supports the MediaTek MT6897 (Dimensity 8300) basic
+	  clocks: the PLLs of apmixedsys, the topckgen and vlpckgen clock
+	  generators and the pericfg_ao clock gates. Some PLLs, muxes and
+	  gates are switched through the hardware voter.
+
+config COMMON_CLK_MT6897_UFSSYS
+	tristate "Clock driver for MediaTek MT6897 ufssys"
+	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6897
+	default COMMON_CLK_MT6897
+	help
+	  This driver supports the MediaTek MT6897 ufscfg_ao and ufscfg_pdn
+	  clock gates, and the UFS M-PHY, UniPro, crypto and host controller
+	  resets found in the same blocks. Say Y or M here when the UFS
+	  storage is used.
+
 config COMMON_CLK_MT7622
 	tristate "Clock driver for MediaTek MT7622"
 	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
